Additional Smart Vacuum Goals

Create a second vacuum agent, separate from the original random-moving vacuum, so both agents can run in the same 10 x 10 Vacuum Cleaner world.
The original Vacuum should keep its existing random behavior.
The new SmartVacuum should inherit from the existing Vacuum agent so it can reuse the same cleaning and movement methods.
Spawn the SmartVacuum at a random in-bounds location each time the simulation starts.
Give SmartVacuum its own color and document that color in the notebook Markdown cell.

Allow the SmartVacuum to perceive the full list of Dirt locations in the grid, while the original Vacuum keeps the default local-only percept behavior.
The SmartVacuum should use the list of Dirt locations to find the closest Dirt object to its current location.
Use grid distance, such as Manhattan distance, to decide which Dirt location is closest.
If SmartVacuum is already on a Dirt location, it should clean that Dirt.
If SmartVacuum is not on Dirt, it should move one step toward the closest Dirt location.
After cleaning a Dirt object, SmartVacuum should repeat the process: update the Dirt list, find the next closest Dirt, move toward it, and clean it.

